  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - U.S.-China Aviation Cooperation Program, through Government of China (P.R.C.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding of $678,000 continued support for the U.S.-China Aviation Cooperation Program (ACP) with an eighth phase. This strategic, multi-program, public-private partnership that USTDA launched in 2004 has produced significant developmental and U.S. export results. Continuation of the program ensured an ongoing high-level dialogue with the Civil Aviation Administration of China (CAAC), which has promoted the interests of the U.S. aviation sector in China. Phase VIII included CAAC executive management training and air traffic management executive training, components that were highly successful in previous phases, as well as Design Seminars for China&apos;s Air Traffic Flow Management.</narrative>
  </description>
